      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Aether Systems is seeing strong engagement within Marketing, where 80% of staff report a robust community sense, yet remote workers face a notable gap in feeling connected to the broader corporate culture. While Engineering enjoys high emotional safety with 65% of teams feeling comfortable being themselves, the lack of mentorship for minority groups remains a critical retention risk that requires an immediate strategic intervention. Leadership must prioritize the 50% calling for more transparency in promotions, as their perception that hiring is only 40% fair indicates a systemic need to refine our selection and advancement processes.\n\nTo address the Infrastructure gaps, we are implementing office accessibility upgrades to boost retention rates for a small but vocal base of 5% expressing physical barriers, while simultaneously launching an \"Inclusion in Action\" program to embed minority-friendly mentorship into Engineering workflows. We aim to validate the positive momentum by publicly highlighting, rather than hiding, our quarterly progress metrics, ensuring we build a culture where every team member feels truly included.\n\n**Inclusivity Index: 6/10**",
      "source": "target",
